# Rule: no bare TODOs

Every `TODO` or `FIXME` comment in code must reference a tracked issue or ticket.

## Good

```
// TODO(ISSUE-123): the rate limiter should fail open during cache outages
// FIXME(JIRA-456): handle the empty-array edge case before the next release
```

## Bad

```
// TODO: clean this up
// FIXME someday
```

## Rationale

A bare `TODO` rots into permanent dead text. Tying every TODO to an issue keeps the backlog honest — if it's not worth filing a ticket, it's not worth a TODO in the code.

## How to apply

When you see a bare TODO/FIXME during review or while writing code, either:

1. Remove it (the work isn't real), or
2. File an issue and append `(ID)` to the comment.

